# Agent & Tools System

## Agent

`Agent` (`src/agent/agent.ts`) is the core orchestrator. It owns:

- A provider-neutral `ProviderAdapter` (OpenRouter cloud by default, or the
  explicit managed local llama.cpp mode). **No AI-SDK / vendor object leaves the
  agent boundary** — enforced by `src/providers/architecture.test.ts`.
- The tool set built by `createTools` (`src/toolset/tools.ts`) plus MCP tools from
  `buildMcpToolSet` (`src/mcp/runtime.ts`).
- Conversation state, context compaction (`src/agent/compaction.ts`), bounded
  repository context (`src/context/compiler.ts`), sub-agent delegation.
- Abort/cancellation and an observer contract that yields `StreamChunk` events
  to the UI / headless output.

### Agent loop

`processMessage` (async generator) streams model output, executes tool calls
via the AI SDK tool runner (bounded by `maxToolRounds`), appends results, and
repeats until no tool calls remain. Observer callbacks
(`onStepStart/onStepFinish/onToolStart/onToolFinish`) drive UI updates.

## Tool interface

AI SDK tools are declared with `tool({ description, inputSchema: z.object(...),
execute })` in `src/toolset/tools.ts`. Internal executors return a `ToolResult`
(`src/types/index.ts`: `{ success, output?, error?, diff?, plan?, ... }`) and
**never throw** — wrap failures in `{ success: false, error }`.

## Built-in tools (grouped)

| Group | Examples |
|-------|----------|
| Shell / process | `bash`, `process_logs`, `process_stop`, `process_list` |
| Files | `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `grep` |
| Code intelligence | `lsp` (when enabled) |
| Sub-agents / tasks | `task`, `delegate`, `delegation_read`, `delegation_list` |
| Schedules / daemon | `schedule_create`, `schedule_list`, `schedule_daemon_*` |
| Computer use | `computer_snapshot`, `computer_click`, `computer_type`, … |
| Search / research | `search_web`, `open_web`, `search_x` |
| Wallet (compat) | `wallet_info`, `wallet_history`, `fetch_payment_info` |

Many tools are gated by capability / settings and only appear when supported.
`search_web` is provider-neutral and the agent performs one bounded research
pass before every task; `open_web` is restricted to public HTTP(S) references.

## Adding a tool

1. Add `name: tool({ description, inputSchema, execute })` in `createTools`
   (`src/toolset/tools.ts`), gating it if it needs a capability.
2. Implement the executor in `src/tools/` returning a `ToolResult`.
3. If the model needs to know about it, update the system prompt in `Agent`.
4. Add a test; keep `bun run typecheck` / `lint` / `test` green.
